'''Truth in Extremes''' (対極にある真実, ''Taikyoku ni Aru Shinjitsu'', '''Truth in Polarity''') is the 7th sub-chapter of [[Zero Legends]], and the 105th sub-chapter overall. It was introduced in [[Version 12.7 Update|Version 12.7]] and is available up to {{2c}} difficulty.

==Difficulty==
A very interesting sub-chapter in terms of difficulty, as all of the even stages have nearly the same contents as their predecessor. The first two stages are pretty straightforward and can be won with relative ease. The next two are harder and might cause some trouble, while the last two are going to be pretty difficult and will require a decent strategy to be done. Evan though the stages are very similar they are very different like [[Blessings in Sand]] and [[Misfortune in Sand]]. [[Blessings in Sand|Blessings in sand]] it contains [[King Wahwah]] a advent boss that is a backliner, but Misfortune in the sand is a [[Mr. Puffington]] type of stage.
{{LegendDiff|120}}

==New Features==
This sub-chapter introduces five enemies to Zero Legends:
*[[Le'mammoth]]: A very tanky event variant of [[Le'boin]] that deals heavy damage, moves faster and has 100% chance to generate a level 3 [[Wave Attack]].
*[[Cosmic Cyclone]]: An [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]]/[[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] enemy with above-average range, lots of health and high DPS. It has a 10% chance to weaken units for 10 seconds and strengthens by 200% at 30% health.
*[[Mini Angel Cyclone]]: A smaller but extremely fast variant of [[Divine Cyclone]] that deals relatively low damage for a [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclone]] but has a 25% chance to generate a level 1 [[Mini-Surge]]; considering her crazy fast attack rate, this will result in the area in front of her being constantly flooded with Mini-Surges. Her health is fairly high, but more so is her amount of knockbacks, which will make her hard to hit for slow attackers, but easy to fend off.
*[[King Wahwah]]: The [[:Category:Advent Bosses|Advent Boss]] of [[N-1 Grand Prix (Deadly)|King Wahwah's Revenge]], this [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] enemy does moderate damage split into three evenly spaced multi-hits, each of which cause knockback. He stands at 600, but his Omni Strike hits up to 1000. Though he has a million health, he is relatively slow and has a whopping 25 knockbacks, so he's easy to ward off if you're able to get to him.
*[[Puffsley's Comet]]: The Advent Boss of [[Puffer Planet (Merciless)|Puffer Planet]] is a souped-up Alien version of [[Mr. Puffington]]. He has below-average health for an Advent Boss, but does extreme damage and, despite standing at 200 range, his Omni Strikes hit up to 500. He sits still for a while after each attack, but will immediately attack again if knocked back, punishing an overaggressive approach. Luring this enemy is not a good idea.

